<title>SWITZERLAND: Von Moos to shed 300 jobs over 18 months.</title>
<headline>Von Moos to shed 300 jobs over 18 months.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Von Moos Holding AG said it would keep steel plants in Emmenbruecke and Gerlafingen in operation but cut 300 jobs over the next 18 months to boost profitability.</p>
<p>Around 1,750 jobs would remain.</p>
<p>Von Moos acquired the Gerlafingen plant from Von Roll last year and had considered closing it and consolidating production at Emmenbruecke. But management said in a statement it would instead specialise output at both plants.</p>
<p>&quot;The assumption that a plant with annual output below 500,000 tonnes cannot be profitable has been disproved by the example of smaller profitable works in Europe,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Combining the two plants would have required around 100 million francs in investment, it added.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
